{"availability":"available","full":"mubin986/CommitArc","name":"CommitArc","description":"Analyze a GitHub repo's commit history and generate technical, client-presentation, or product-demo AI reports with Claude — edit in a Notion-style editor, present as slides, export to Markdown/PPTX/PDF, and publish to Gist/Wiki/Release.","category":"Design","language":"TypeScript","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2026-06-19T06:20:07Z","updated":"2026-06-22T10:00:50Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://mubin986.github.io/CommitArc/","topics":["ai","anthropic","changelog","claude","commit-history","developer-tools","gh-cli","github","llm","nextjs","react","report-generator","tailwindcss","typescript"],"demo":"https://mubin986.github.io/CommitArc/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T22:40:55.760Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-11T22:40:55.760Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-11T22:40:55.760Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T22:40:55.760Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":["React","Next.js"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Analyze a GitHub repository's commit history over a date range or up to a tag, then generate an AI report with Claude — either a technical engineering summary or a client-facing presentation. Works with public and private repos.","gh is the lowest-friction option for a local/personal tool and is what this app defaults to for private repos. GITHUBTOKEN is the portable fallback (e.g. if you deploy to Vercel, where gh doesn't exist). If you ever host CommitArc for multiple users, the right upgrade is GitHub OAuth so each visitor authorizes their own access — not implemented here."],"features":["Paste any GitHub repo URL ( git@…, or owner/repo).","Date range — since / until (+ optional branch).","Up to a tag — compare baseTag → tag, or list all commits reachable from a single tag.","Aggregate stats: total commits, additions/deletions, file changes, per-contributor activity.","Per-commit diff stats (additions/d